<title>USA: Timberland Co Q4 net, share rise.</title>
<headline>Timberland Co Q4 net, share rise.</headline>
<dateline>STRATHAM, N.H. 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Amounts in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>				  For the		    For the</p>
<p>			   Three Months Ended   Twelve Months Ended</p>
<p>				 Dec 31, Dec 31,    Dec 31,   Dec 31,</p>
<p>				    1996    1995	 1996     1995</p>
<p> Revenues		   $221,094 $175,815  $689,973  $655,138</p>
<p> Cost of goods sold	138,592  117,025   438,064   451,741</p>
<p>   Gross profit	     82,502  58,790    251,909   203,397</p>
<p>Operating expenses</p>
<p>   Selling		    46,260  39,870    152,834   145,924</p>
<p>General and</p>
<p>     administrative	 13,665  11,731     46,502    46,721</p>
<p>Amortization of</p>
<p>     goodwill		    421     421	1,684     1,685</p>
<p>   Restructuring charge	  -	 -	    -    16,000</p>
<p>Total operating</p>
<p>	  expenses	    60,346  52,022    201,020   210,330</p>
<p>Operating income</p>
<p>	   (loss)	     22,156   6,768     50,889   (6,933)</p>
<p>Other expense (income)</p>
<p>   Interest expense	  5,439   5,561     20,582    22,861</p>
<p>   Other, net		  (515)    (16)	(631)  (11,028)</p>
<p>     Total other expense   4,924   5,545     19,951    11,833</p>
<p>Income (loss) before</p>
<p>	   income taxes     17,232   1,223     30,938  (18,766)</p>
<p>Provision (benefit) for</p>
<p>   income taxes		5,859     464     10,519   (7,131)</p>
<p>    Net income (loss)     11,373     759     20,419  (11,635)</p>
<p>Earnings (loss)</p>
<p>    per share		    .99     .07	 1.81    (1.04)</p>
<p>Weighted average shares</p>
<p>     outstanding	    11,462  11,165     11,255    11,171</p>
<p>NOTES: The 1995 loss included two significant, non-recurring items, a pre-tax charge of $16.0 million for a manufacturing restructuring, and a pre-tax gain of $12.1 million for the appointment of Inchcape plc as Timberland's distributor in the Asia/Pacific region.  The net impact of these two items, both of which occurred prior to the fourth quarter of 1995, was a $0.22 per share loss after taxes.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
